# Line endings for the files that leave this repository and run somewhere else.
#
# `ops/capacity-sampler.sh` and its two systemd units are installed onto Ubuntu
# straight from a checkout, by the scp block in `ops/capacity-measurement.md`.
# `core.autocrlf` is true on the authoring machine, so without the rules below a
# fresh clone hands those files to `scp` with CRLF endings. Bash then fails with
# `$'\r': command not found` and systemd mis-parses a unit file's last value on
# every line, which is the kind of break that looks like a box problem rather
# than a checkout problem.
#
# Deliberately narrow. A repository-wide `* text=auto` would renormalise files
# no story has touched, which is a large unrelated diff.

*.sh text eol=lf
*.service text eol=lf
*.timer text eol=lf
*.mjs text eol=lf

# `contracts/` is the published surface. It is vendored into seven repositories
# under one fixed folder name (AD-14), it is generated with `\n` endings by
# `packages/tokens/build.mjs`, and the `tokens-contract` CI job fails on any
# difference between the committed file and a fresh build. Without this rule a
# checkout on the authoring machine holds CRLF, and whether the gate agrees with
# the generator would depend on whose `core.autocrlf` ran last.
contracts/** text eol=lf
